(PMAs), New Drug Applications (NDAs) or 510Ks.\nL92: ### Biologics License Applications and Supplements\nL93: \nL94: New BLAs (except those for blood banking), and BLA supplements that are expected to significantly enhance the public health (e.g., for new/expanded indications, new routes of administration, new dosage formulations and improved safety).\nL95:   * 【55†2022 Biological License Application Approvals】\nL96:   * 【56†2022 Biological License Application Supplement Noteworthy Approvals】\nL97:   * 【57†2022 Biological New Drug Application (NDA) and Abbreviated New Drug Application (ANDA) Approvals】\nL98: ### Other Applications Approved or Cleared by the Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research (CBER)\nL99: \nL100: Medical devices involved in the collection, processing, testing, manufacture and administration of licensed blood, blood components and cellular products.\nL101: \nL102:   * 【58†2022 Biological Device Application Approvals】\nL103: ### Key Resources\nL104: \nL105:   * 【42†Development & Approval Process (CBER)】\nL106:   * 【59†Biologics Products & Establishments】\nL107:   * 【60†Transfer of Therapeutic Products to the Center for Drug Evaluation and Research - Archived】\nL108: ## Footer Links\nL109: \nL110:   * 【61†FDA Archive】\nL111:   * 【27†About FDA】\nL112:   * 【62†Accessibility】\nL113: \nL114:   * 【63†Visitor Information】\nL115:   * 【64†Website Policies / Privacy】\nL116:   * 【65†No FEAR Act】\nL117:   * 【66†Vulnerability Disclosure Policy】\nL118: \nL119:   * 【67†FOIA】\nL120:   * 【68†HHS.gov】\nL121:   * 【69†USA.gov】\nL122: \nL123: 【12†Contact FDA】 【70†Follow FDA on Facebook】 【71†Follow FDA on X】 【72†Follow FDA on Instagram】\nL124: 【73†Follow FDA on LinkedIn】 【74†View FDA videos on YouTube】 【75†Subscribe to FDA RSS feeds】\nL125: \nL126: 【9†FDA Homepage】\nL127: \nL128: Contact Number 1-888-INFO-FDA (1-888-463-6332)\nL129: Back to Top\n"
